
  [1mWhat changed from the original request[0m

  The one-line ask turned into a design because two things didn't hold up:

  - [1mA [38;5;153muserId[39m parameter has nothing to pass it.[0m No user ID exists in this app, so the caller can't supply one. [38;5;153muserId[39m is
    an [3moutput[0m of authentication — the spec returns it from [38;5;153mlogin()[39m rather than accepting it.
  - [1m[38;5;153mlogin()[39m authenticates nobody.[0m It returns [38;5;153m{success: true}[39m for any input and never contacts the network. Server-side
    login tracking is impossible until that's real, so making it real is the actual work — and it's a security fix, not
    a feature.

  The tracking you asked about lives in the auth endpoint, server-side. That's backend work and explicitly out of scope
  here.

  [1mSelf-review found three real problems, fixed inline[0m

  - [1m401 matched two error rows.[0m 401 is non-2xx, so it also satisfied the [38;5;153mserver_error[39m condition. The table is now
    explicitly ordered, first-match-wins, with the ordering called out as load-bearing.
  - [1m"Usable [38;5;153muserId[39m" was undefined[0m — it now has one definition (non-empty trimmed string) referenced everywhere, plus a
    test case for [38;5;153muserId: ""[39m, which a truthiness check wrongly rejects and a [38;5;153m!== undefined[39m check wrongly accepts.
  - [1mThe credential-leak check was listed as a test case[0m but is really an assertion across all cases. Restated as a
    shared helper.

  [1mThree risks worth your attention[0m

  1. [1mThe wire contract is unratified.[0m I proposed the 200/401/5xx shapes; no backend has agreed to them. Mock-based tests
     pass regardless of whether the contract is right, so they offer no protection against a mismatch.
  2. [1mNothing runs end-to-end.[0m [38;5;153mapi.example.com[39m is a placeholder.
  3. [1m[38;5;153mfile://[39m stops working.[0m [38;5;153mtype="module"[39m is CORS-blocked on [38;5;153mfile://[39m, so opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m directly in a browser will
     break — the page will need serving over HTTP. A genuine workflow regression, accepted as the cost of approach A.

  Please review the spec and tell me if you want changes. Once you approve it, the next step is the writing-plans skill
  to produce the implementation plan — I won't write code before then.

